# --- pix-key, added by the security audit ---
# Phone numbers and a UUID that a fuzzer turned up, now fixtures. The phone one
# is the case that matters: every Brazilian number in E.164 form begins with 55,
# which is inside the Mastercard issuer range 51-55, so a +55 number whose
# digits happen to satisfy Luhn was being reported as a credit card.
007c91df5488278b2c7164c16d4f04d4  # +***********75 - the number the fuzzer minimized to
a83871a7916f6b9c44907082aa289cfc  # +***********21 - a second phone in the same shape
d554cea51a6155fd70c74664b448aff2  # +***********94 - a third
9ee2bb2c7f2a591ab50bb3070faa1a6d  # a UUID v4 Pix key, in the overlap test

# --- test fixtures outside the corpus ---
# Values the mask and hook tests use. The same values also sit in corpus/cases/,
# which the path rule below covers; these lines cover the test files.
d0dead6eceff137cafd15c0029bf1214  # AKIA...LE example key, cmd/vedei-hook/main_test.go
2040ad664a71a504a6ff863b0b78a4f0  # generated PIS vector, space-separated, detect/br/extract_test.go
62949e15935851bd24d617292e7230f8  # generated titulo vector, space-separated, detect/br/extract_test.go
ec2a7642f9821664294f09e54573ca66  # generated CNS vector, detect/br/extract_test.go
c3fca3e7a0151668ec85c974b0f4f57f  # the made-up credential from the corpus, also in transcript/stats_test.go
3d916d891e1aab79bc68592c2d7cd3a5  # the first alphanumeric CNPJ the Receita issued; an earlier version of this file quoted it in a comment, so git history still holds it

# --- the one path rule: the labeled corpus ---
# Everything else in this file is a single value, named, and that is the rule:
# silencing *_test.go wholesale would also silence a credential genuinely
# committed into a test, which is a place credentials genuinely end up.
#
# corpus/cases/ is the one exception. It exists to hold labeled example values,
# and the corpus test fails on any line that is not an "expect" or a "reject",
# so a value there is a labeled case by construction. Naming each one here
# would mean a fingerprint per case — hundreds, at the size M5 aims for — each
# one easy to forget. History and diff scans honour this rule too.
corpus/cases/
